-- title:
--   Index of lattices is the product of local indices
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring which is a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra, and let $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $D$. Assume each is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module and spans $D$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, i.e. the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of the underlying set of $\Lambda_i$ is all of $D$ for $i=1,2$, and assume $\Lambda_2\le\Lambda_1$. Then the relative index of $\Lambda_2$ in $\Lambda_1$, taken for the underlying additive subgroups (so the cardinality of $\Lambda_1/(\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2)=\Lambda_1/\Lambda_2$, as a natural number), equals the finitely supported product, over the height one primes $v$ of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, of the relative index of [`Submodule.localBox Λ₂ v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) in [`Submodule.localBox Λ₁ v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40). Here [`Submodule.localBox Λ v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) is, for a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda$ of $D$, the additive subgroup of $D\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elementary tensors $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of the $v$-adic completion of $\mathbb{Q}$. The product is an unrestricted (`finprod`) product, so the assertion includes implicitly that all but finitely many local indices are $1$.
--
--   This is the standard local–global formula $[\Lambda_1:\Lambda_2]=\prod_v[\Lambda_{1,v}:\Lambda_{2,v}]$ for full $\mathbb{Z}$-lattices in a finite-dimensional $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra, here with the local lattices presented as the additive subgroups generated by $\Lambda\otimes\mathcal{O}_v$ inside $D\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$. It is used in the quaternionic part of the argument to recognise intersections of orders obtained from Hecke translates as Eichler orders of the expected level, by computing indices one prime at a time.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Submodule_relIndex_toAddSubgroup_eq_finprod_relIndex_localBox.lean

